{"kind":"stack","id":"s-shadows","title":"Shadows: light blocked by opaque objects","theme":{"background":"#1d2b3a","foreground":"#ffffff","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"What is needed to make a shadow?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"A light source and an opaque object","why":"A shadow forms when an opaque object blocks light from a light source.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Two light sources","why":"Pupils may think more light always makes a shadow, but light must be blocked.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"A transparent object and a dark room","why":"Pupils may think a dark room alone creates shadows, but there must be light to block.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Opaque"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"An opaque object does not let light pass through it, so it blocks the light and makes a shadow."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-n","label":"Next Card","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which object makes the biggest shadow?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"A wooden block","why":"A solid opaque block blocks all the light from that side, so it casts a clear shadow.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"A clear glass of water","why":"Pupils may think water always makes shadows, but clear glass lets light pass through.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"A sheet of tissue paper","why":"Pupils may think any paper blocks light, but thin tissue lets most light through.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Why does a shadow form behind your hand when the sun shines on it?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Your hand blocks the sunlight","why":"The opaque hand stops sunlight, so the area behind it stays dark.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Your hand makes new light","why":"Pupils may think hands produce light, but they only block it.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"The sun turns off behind your hand","why":"Pupils may think the sun stops in one place, but the sun keeps shining.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"You are walking home on a sunny day. Your shadow is very long. Do you race ahead to see it or stop to play with it?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Race ahead","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Stop to play","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You race ahead. Your shadow stretches on the path because the low sun is shining from behind you."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-n","label":"Continue","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"You stop and wave your arms. Your shadow waves too, because your body blocks the sunlight."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-n","label":"Continue","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Which material is opaque?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Cardboard","why":"Cardboard does not let light pass through, so it is opaque.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Clear plastic","why":"Pupils may think all plastic is the same, but clear plastic lets light through.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Window glass","why":"Pupils may think glass always blocks light, but window glass is transparent.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"If you move a torch closer to an object, what happens to its shadow?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"It gets bigger","why":"A closer light spreads out more, so the shadow grows larger.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"It gets smaller","why":"Pupils may think closer means smaller, but a close light makes a bigger shadow.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"It disappears","why":"Pupils may think a shadow needs distance, but the object still blocks the light.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"What is a shadow?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"A dark area where light is blocked","why":"A shadow is the dark area behind an object that blocks light.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"A light that moves across a wall","why":"Pupils may mix up shadows with light patches, but a shadow is a dark area.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"A reflection in a mirror","why":"Pupils may confuse reflections and shadows, but a reflection bounces light back.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"You finished the shadows lesson!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Well done. Shadows form when opaque objects block light from a light source."}],"actions":[]}}
